1
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
MAYA: The letter says the lighthouse is mine now. Grandpa left it to me.

2
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:12,477
LEO: Maya, that's amazing! You always loved that place.

3
00:00:12,877 --> 00:00:17,492
- It also says there's a debt. Forty thousand, due in thirty days.

4
00:00:17,892 --> 00:00:20,969
LEO: Hey. Don't worry. We'll figure it out together.

5
00:00:21,369 --> 00:00:25,215
LEO: Here, take my savings. It's not much, but it's yours.

6
00:00:25,615 --> 00:00:27,538
- Leo, I can't take that.

7
00:00:27,938 --> 00:00:31,015
LEO: You can. That's what friends are for. [chuckles]

8
00:00:40,415 --> 00:00:42,723
VICTOR: Miss Calder. I represent Harbor Developments.

9
00:00:43,123 --> 00:00:46,200
- We'd like to buy the lighthouse. Today. Cash.

10
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,200
MAYA: It's not for sale.

11
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:52,831
VICTOR: Everything is for sale when the bank calls in a debt.

12
00:00:53,231 --> 00:00:55,538
- Mr. Kade, the car is waiting.

13
00:00:55,938 --> 00:00:58,631
VICTOR: Think about it. Thirty days goes fast.

14
00:01:08,031 --> 00:01:12,262
MAYA: Who sends a man in a suit to a lighthouse? [laughs]

15
00:01:12,662 --> 00:01:14,969
- Someone who wants it very badly.

16
00:01:15,369 --> 00:01:20,369
LEO: I asked around at the harbor. Kade bought every building on this coast.

17
00:01:20,769 --> 00:01:23,846
MAYA: Why would he care about one old tower?

18
00:01:24,246 --> 00:01:29,246
- I don't know. But I'll stay with you tonight. You shouldn't be alone.

19
00:01:29,646 --> 00:01:31,246
MAYA: Thank you, Leo. Really.

20
00:01:40,646 --> 00:01:44,108
INES: Sir, these papers from the archive mention the lighthouse.

21
00:01:44,508 --> 00:01:46,108
- Put them away, Ines.

22
00:01:46,508 --> 00:01:50,738
INES: They say your father and her grandfather built the harbor together.

23
00:01:51,138 --> 00:01:53,062
VICTOR: I said put them away!

24
00:01:53,462 --> 00:01:57,308
- He was your partner. And you never paid him back.

25
00:01:57,708 --> 00:01:59,631
VICTOR: That debt died with him.

26
00:02:00,031 --> 00:02:03,877
INES: Did it? Or is that why you want the tower?

27
00:02:13,277 --> 00:02:16,354
♪ Storm winds rising, lantern burning bright ♪

28
00:02:16,754 --> 00:02:21,369
MAYA: The lamp is still working. Grandpa kept it running for forty years.

29
00:02:21,769 --> 00:02:25,231
LEO: Look at this. A ledger, hidden under the stairs.

30
00:02:25,631 --> 00:02:28,708
- It's full of names. Ships he guided home.

31
00:02:29,108 --> 00:02:32,954
LEO: And one page about a loan. To someone called Kade.

32
00:02:33,354 --> 00:02:37,585
MAYA: So it's Kade who owes us, not the other way around?

33
00:02:46,985 --> 00:02:49,292
- Miss Calder? I shouldn't be here.

34
00:02:49,692 --> 00:02:53,154
INES: My boss lied to you. The debt was forged.

35
00:02:53,554 --> 00:02:55,862
MAYA: Why are you telling me this?

36
00:02:56,262 --> 00:03:00,877
- Because your grandfather saved my father's boat in the storm of '88.

37
00:03:01,277 --> 00:03:05,892
INES: Here. Copies of the original contract. Don't tell him it was me.

38
00:03:06,292 --> 00:03:08,600
LEO: You're risking your job for us.

39
00:03:08,1000 --> 00:03:11,308
- Some debts matter more than jobs.

40
00:03:20,708 --> 00:03:22,631
VICTOR: You've been busy, Miss Calder.

41
00:03:23,031 --> 00:03:28,415
MAYA: Your father borrowed from my grandfather. You forged the debt to steal the tower.

42
00:03:28,815 --> 00:03:30,415
- You can't prove that.

43
00:03:30,815 --> 00:03:35,046
LEO: We can. The ledger and the contract say the same thing.

44
00:03:35,446 --> 00:03:42,369
VICTOR: [sighs] My father talked about him every day. Said he was the only honest man on the coast.

45
00:03:42,769 --> 00:03:47,769
- I wanted the tower so I'd never have to hear his name again.

46
00:03:48,169 --> 00:03:51,631
MAYA: Then pay what you owe. And keep his name.

47
00:03:52,031 --> 00:03:55,492
VICTOR: ...I'm sorry. I'll cancel the debt. All of it.

48
00:04:04,892 --> 00:04:06,815
- So. A lighthouse keeper, huh?

49
00:04:07,215 --> 00:04:10,677
MAYA: Only if my best friend helps me paint it.

50
00:04:11,077 --> 00:04:14,923
LEO: Deal. But I'm not climbing those stairs every day. [laughs]

51
00:04:15,323 --> 00:04:18,785
- Ines is coming for dinner. She deserves a thank-you.

52
00:04:19,185 --> 00:04:21,877
LEO: The lamp still works. Let's light it.

53
00:04:22,277 --> 00:04:23,877
MAYA: For Grandpa.
